**Headline findings:**

- **Central default estimate: ~15%** (range 12-19%), above Passage's 10% base but below 25% pessimistic
- **10% is defensible as a conditional best case** (full employment assumption), not as an unconditional central
- **The case is remarkably robust**: money comes back up to 32.5% default; GiveWell bar holds to ~42%
- **Year 2 clinical crunch is the discrete default mechanism** — payment/income ratio of 102-203% during clinical placement creates forced arrears that compound
- **Top structural fix**: clinical placement payment pause (estimated -3-5pp default reduction, near-zero cost to financial model)
- **Default risk is NOT the decision-relevant risk** — the 11.95% APR self-hedges credit defaults up to extraordinary levels; only correlated systemic failure (immigration policy + nursing market) breaks both sides simultaneously
